  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Situation Room</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WSR  Project aims to contribute to a peaceful and inclusive electoral process in Somaliland, with a particular focus on promoting women&apos;s participation and addressing the root causes of past electoral violence. Elections in Somaliland have historically been marred by violence, particularly affecting marginalized groups such as youth and women. The recent postponement of the parliamentary elections has raised concerns about the credibility of the electoral process and the potential for further unrest.

This project seeks to address these challenges by:
&#x2022; Promoting peaceful elections: Raising awareness among citizens about the importance of peacefulelections and addressing the root causes of past violence.
&#x2022; Enhancing women&apos;s participation: Supporting women&apos;s involvement in theelectoral process as candidates, voters, and advocates.
&#x2022; Strengthening the electoral process: Improving the credibility and inclusivity of the electoral process through targeted interventions.

Objectives
&#x2022; To promote a peaceful and inclusive electoral process in Somaliland.
&#x2022; To enhance women&apos;s participation in the electoral process.
&#x2022; To strengthen the credibility and inclusivity of the electoral process.

 Expected Outcomes
&#x2022; Increased awareness among citizens about the importance of peaceful elections.
&#x2022; Enhanced participation of women in the electoral process as candidates, voters, and advocates.
&#x2022; Improved credibility and inclusivity of the electoral process.
&#x2022; Reduced incidence of electoral violence.

Expected Outputs
&#x2022; Trained media actors
&#x2022; Conducted women&apos;s campaign andadvocacy workshops
&#x2022; Boosted and implemented WSR guideline
&#x2022; Increased media coverage of women&apos;s participation in the electoral process
&#x2022; Reduced reports of electoral violence

The project will be implemented from October 1, 2024 to December 31, 2024 with a budget of USD 31,280</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NAGAAD Network</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nagaad is the women#s network in Somaliland, which ON has been supporting since its establishment in1997. Nagaad was formed by 32 women#s groups in Hargeisa. While it has raised its profile tremendously after 2000, with a range of advocacy and publicity actions in the media, notably around women#s political participation, it has always remained a  of 32 member organisations, many of them remain weak, except for a few larger ones (some of whom are also counterparts of Oxfam Novib). Nagaad built its own office and received support from a variety of donors. Over the last four years Nagaad has elaborated a restructuring plan and a new strategic plan that involves: (a) more focus on networking instead of direct implementation; (b) admission of 15 new members from the regions of Somaliland, and working relationships with regional women#s umbrellas and professional associations. The network now has a membership of 46organisations.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
